# Structure

## Core Directories
- app/ (Expo Router app directory)
  - _layout.tsx (root layout with theme and navigation setup)
  - (tabs)/ (tab-based navigation)
  - article/ (article-related screens)
- components/ (reusable UI components)
- constants/ (enums, constants, configuration)
- hooks/ (reusable React hooks)
- store/ (Redux store and slices)
- services/ (API and external service integrations)
- types/ (TypeScript type definitions)
  - *.types.ts (type definitions for specific features)
  - database.types.ts (database schema types)

## Assets and Config
- assets/ (static assets like fonts and images)
- .cursor/ (AI assistant rules and configuration)

# Stack

## Core Technologies
- Expo (latest version)
- React Native
- TypeScript
- Redux Toolkit for state management
- Expo Router for navigation
- React Query for data fetching

## Development Guidelines
- Use Expo features and APIs when available
- Use modern React patterns (hooks, functional components)
- Use Redux for global state, never Context API
- Use TypeScript strictly - avoid any

# General

## Code Style
- Keep code DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions
- Write simple, readable code
- Minimize comments - write self-documenting code
- Follow existing patterns in the codebase

## Project Structure
- Keep files in appropriate directories based on their purpose
- Create new files in existing directories
- Don't create new top-level directories without discussion
- Use feature-based organization within directories

# React and React Native

## Component Guidelines
- Use functional components
- Use TypeScript interfaces for props
- Avoid inline styles - use StyleSheet.create
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Don't use console.log in production code

## Data Fetching
- Use React Query for API calls
- Define services in services/ directory
- Define types in types/ directory
- Handle loading and error states

# Colors and Theming

## Theme System
- Theme state is managed by Redux via themeSlice
- System theme is automatically synced unless explicitly overridden
- All colors are defined in constants/Colors.ts for both light and dark themes
- Colors are accessed via the useColors hook

## Using Colors in Components
- Always use the useColors hook from @/hooks/useColors
  ```typescript
  const colors = useColors();
  ```
- Never use Colors constants or useColorScheme directly
- All components must support both light and dark themes
- When adding new colors:
  1. Add to both light and dark themes in Colors.ts
  2. Add TypeScript types if needed

## ThemedText Component
- Use skipDefaultColor when providing custom colors:
  ```typescript
  // For custom colored text
  <ThemedText 
    style={[styles.category, { color: colors.categoryText }]}
    skipDefaultColor
  >
    {text}
  </ThemedText>

  // For default text color
  <ThemedText style={styles.title}>
    {text}
  </ThemedText>
  ```
- The component automatically handles default text colors if skipDefaultColor is not set

## Theme State Management
- Theme changes are handled in app/_layout.tsx
- System theme changes are automatically applied
- Theme state persists across app restarts
- Theme can be manually controlled via the setTheme action:
  ```typescript
  dispatch(setTheme(Theme.Dark)); // or Theme.Light
  ```
